text: ['({T}: Add {G}.)', '({T}: Add {U}.)', '({T}: Add {W}.)', 'Battle cry (Whenever this creature attacks, each other attacking creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn.)', 'Choose target creature an opponent controls. When that creature dies this turn, you gain 3 life. Target creature you control fights that creature. (Each deals damage equal to its power to the other.)', "Counter target spell. At the beginning of your next precombat main phase, add X mana in any combination of colors, where X is that spell's mana value.", 'Create X 4/4 white Angel creature tokens with flying.\\nCycling {2}{W} ({2}{W}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)\\nWhen you cycle Decree of Justice, you may pay {X}. If you do, create X 1/1 white Soldier creature tokens.', 'Create two 1/1 white Soldier creature tokens.', 'Cycling {2}{W} ({2}{W}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)\\nWhen you cycle Gempalm Avenger, Soldier creatures get +1/+1 and gain first strike until end of turn.', 'Draw a card, then draw cards equal to the number of cards named Accumulated Knowledge in all graveyards.', 'Draw three cards. You may play an additional land this turn.', 'First strike\\nWhenever Precinct Captain deals combat damage to a player, create a 1/1 white Soldier creature token.', 'Flash\\nCreatures you control get +2/+2.', "Flying, trample\\nShroud (This creature can't be the target of spells or abilities.)", 'Flying\\nNimbus Swimmer enters the battlefield with X +1/+1 counters on it.', "Flying\\nWhen Kor Skyfisher enters the battlefield, return a permanent you control to its owner's hand.", 'Flying\\nWhenever Gustcloak Harrier becomes blocked, you may untap it and remove it from combat.', 'Flying\\nWhenever Gustcloak Skirmisher becomes blocked, you may untap it and remove it from combat.', 'Flying\\nWhenever a creature you control becomes blocked, you may untap that creature and remove it from combat.', 'Icatian Javelineers enters the battlefield with a javelin counter on it.\\n{T}, Remove a javelin counter from Icatian Javelineers: It deals 1 damage to any target.', 'Landfall — Whenever a land enters the battlefield under your control, you may gain 2 life.', 'Other Soldier creatures you control get +0/+1.', 'Other Soldier creatures you control get +1/+0.', 'Prevent all damage one or two target creatures would deal this turn.', 'Reach (This creature can block creatures with flying.)\\nWhenever Netcaster Spider blocks a creature with flying, Netcaster Spider gets +2/+0 until end of turn.', "Reach\\n{6}{G}: Monstrosity 4. (If this creature isn't monstrous, put four +1/+1 counters on it and it becomes monstrous.)", "Return all attacking creatures to their owner's hand.", "Return all creatures to their owners' hands except for Krakens, Leviathans, Octopuses, and Serpents.", "Return target creature you control and target creature you don't control to their owners' hands.", "Sealock Monster can't attack unless defending player controls an Island.\\n{5}{U}{U}: Monstrosity 3. (If this creature isn't monstrous, put three +1/+1 counters on it and it becomes monstrous.)\\nWhen Sealock Monster becomes monstrous, target land becomes an Island in addition to its other types.", 'Search your library for up to two basic land cards, put them onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', 'Secluded Steppe enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {W}.\\nCycling {W} ({W}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', 'Sunlance deals 3 damage to target nonwhite creature.', 'Target creature gets +1/+1 and gains lifelink until end of turn. (Damage dealt by the creature also causes its controller to gain that much life.)', 'Target creature gets +2/+2 and gains flying until end of turn.', 'Target player sacrifices an attacking or blocking creature.', "Trample\\nIslandwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls an Island.)\\nShroud (This creature can't be the target of spells or abilities.)", 'Up to two target creatures each get +2/+2 until end of turn.', 'Vigilance', "Vigilance (Attacking doesn't cause this creature to tap.)\\nOther Soldier creatures you control get +1/+1 and have vigilance.\\nWhen Captain of the Watch enters the battlefield, create three 1/1 white Soldier creature tokens.", 'Vigilance\\nPlainscycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Search your library for a Plains card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.)', "When Banisher Priest enters the battlefield, exile target creature an opponent controls until Banisher Priest leaves the battlefield. (That creature returns under its owner's control.)", "When Coiling Oracle enters the battlefield, reveal the top card of your library. If it's a land card, put it onto the battlefield. Otherwise, put that card into your hand.", 'When Kinsbaile Skirmisher enters the battlefield, target creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', "When Man-o'-War enters the battlefield, return target creature to its owner's hand.", 'When Omenspeaker enters the battlefield, scry 2. (Look at the top two cards of your library, then put any number of them on the bottom of your library and the rest on top in any order.)', "When Scourge of Fleets enters the battlefield, return each creature your opponents control with toughness X or less to its owner's hand, where X is the number of Islands you control.", "When Surrakar Banisher enters the battlefield, you may return target tapped creature to its owner's hand.", 'Whenever Gustcloak Sentinel becomes blocked, you may untap it and remove it from combat.', 'Whenever another white creature enters the battlefield under your control, tap target creature an opponent controls.', 'Whenever you draw a card, put a +1/+1 counter on Lorescale Coatl.', 'You may play an additional land this turn.\\nDraw a card.', '[+1]: Create three 1/1 white Soldier creature tokens.\\n[−3]: Destroy all creatures with power 4 or greater.\\n[−7]: You get an emblem with "Creatures you control get +2/+2 and have flying."', '[+1]: Until your next turn, prevent all damage that would be dealt to and dealt by target permanent an opponent controls.\\n[−1]: Draw a card. You may play an additional land this turn.\\n[−5]: You get an emblem with "At the beginning of your end step, create a 9/9 blue Kraken creature token."', '{T}, Sacrifice Evolving Wilds: Search your library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', '{T}: Add {C}{C}. Activate only if you control five or more lands.', '{T}: Target creature you control gains protection from the color of your choice until end of turn.', '{T}: Untap another target permanent.']
flavor: ['"Bant sentries were called the Angel Line. They never faltered, and they were ready to die defending their position."\\n—Elspeth', '"Beauty to the eye does not always translate to the touch."\\n—Naimah, Femeref philosopher', '"Courage is a proud and gleaming shield. It does not bend or hide from sight. To fight with courage, we must forge in steel."', '"Don\'t be fooled. If it were as docile as it looks, it would\'ve died off long ago."\\n—Yon Basrel, Oran-Rief survivalist', '"Everything serves a purpose. Even you."\\n—Vorel of the Hull Clade', '"I can see why this appeals to Thassa."\\n—Kiora', '"I was called to this world of steel, and it will be my steel that answers."\\n—Elspeth', '"I will never run out of new oceans to explore or new sea-dwellers to embrace as my own."\\n—Kiora', '"If a boggart even dares breathe near one of my kin, I\'ll know. And I\'ll not be happy."', '"In our war Heliod gave mortals some favor, yet other times he withheld aid. Are we still no more than game pieces to him?"\\n—Polyxene the Doubter', '"In troubled times, we all need someone to watch our back."', '"Into its maw went the seventh sea, never to be seen again while the world remains."\\n—Esper fable', '"It\'s easy for the innocent to speak of justice. They seldom feel its terrible power."\\n—Orim, Samite inquisitor', '"Learn not only from the failures of the past, but also from its triumphs."\\n—Isperia', '"Nature was slowly heading in the right direction, but we know how to achieve faster results."\\n—Vorel of the Hull Clade', '"Oathbreaker, I cast you out!"', '"On every plane I\'ve encountered loxodons, I\'ve found stalwart and loyal friends."\\n—Elspeth', '"Our death-arrows flew in high arcs towards the aven. And then . . . nothing."\\n—Coliseum guard', '"She may call herself Kiora but I believe she is Thassa, the embodiment of the sea and empress of the depths."', '"Sometimes I snare the unexpected, but I know its purpose will be revealed in time."', '"Soulless demon, you are bound to me. Now we will both dwell in oblivion."', '"Such deeds should be common fare for such as us."\\n—Anax, king of Akros', '"The Boros fight for justice. The Azorius fight for law. I hold the line between, and make sure the people are given both."', '"The enlightenment I never found in etherium I have found traced in the coatl\'s scales."\\n—Ranalus, vedalken heretic', '"The people of Akros must learn from our leonin adversaries. If we match their staunch ferocity with our superior faith, we cannot fail."\\n—Cymede, queen of Akros', '"The southern fortress taken by invaders? Heh, sure . . . when elephants fly."\\n—Brezard Skeinbow, captain of the guard', '"Truth is a straight, keen edge. There are no soft angles or rounded edges. To fight for truth, we must forge in steel."', '"We\'ve bred out the shortcomings of the species\' natural form and replaced them with assets of our own design."\\n—Momir Vig', '"When gods become apathetic, the people will worship anyone who answers their pleas."\\n—Kiora', '"You can come back once you\'ve learned some manners—and figured out how to reconstitute your physical forms."', '"You were defeated the moment you declared your aggression."\\n—Gideon Jura', 'As the Simic released more of their krasis experiments, they required new habitats, always at the expense of the locals.', 'Banking steeply, the aven streaked toward the ground—and vanished.', 'Entire platoons have mysteriously vanished from battle, leaving enemy weapons to slice through empty air.', 'Her prophecies amaze her even as she speaks them.', 'It is an expert at culling individuals who stray too far from the herd.', "It's not the two heads you should fear. It's the four fangs.", 'Like blinking or breathing, responding to an alarm is an involuntary reflex.', 'She will not touch a weapon, yet she is the greatest protector her people have ever known.', "Surrakar grab things they *don't* want.", 'The Simic soon discovered that the sky offered as few constraints on size as the sea.', "They're trained in the art of pressing their luck.", 'Torching Krosa would be pointless. It grows faster than it burns.', 'Without the interfering hands of civilization, nature will always shape itself to its own needs.']
artist: ['Adam Paquette', 'Alex Horley-Orlandelli', 'Anthony Francisco', 'Chase Stone', 'Clint Cearley', 'Dallas Williams', 'Dan Frazier', 'Dan Murayama Scott', 'David Palumbo', 'Eric Deschamps', 'Eytan Zana', 'Greg Staples', 'Heather Hudson', 'Howard Lyon', 'Igor Kieryluk', 'James Zapata', 'Jason Felix', 'Jim Nelson', 'Johann Bodin', 'John Avon', 'Jon J Muth', 'Kev Walker', 'Lius Lasahido', 'Mark Zug', 'Matt Cavotta', 'Matt Stewart', 'Michael Komarck', 'Michael Phillippi', 'Peter Mohrbacher', 'Raoul Vitale', 'Rob Alexander', 'Ryan Barger', 'Ryan Pancoast', 'Slawomir Maniak', 'Steve Prescott', 'Steven Belledin', 'Terese Nielsen', 'Thomas Denmark', 'Tim Hildebrandt', 'Tyler Jacobson', 'Volkan Baǵa', 'Wayne Reynolds', 'Willian Murai', 'Yohann Schepacz', 'Zoltan Boros', 'rk post']
